---
import DocLayout from "../../../layouts/DocLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<DocLayout
  title="Local MCP quickstart"
  description="Copy-paste setup for running rob-mcp as a free local stdio MCP server with Bun or plain Node and your own Robinhood Chain RPC."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Getting started</p><h1>Run rob-mcp locally</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Local stdio MCP is free. It talks directly to your configured RPC and does not use the hosted
    x402 paywall.
  </p>
  <h2>1. Provide an RPC</h2>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`export RPC_URL_4663="https://your-robinhood-chain-rpc.example"`}
    label="Required environment"
  />
  <h2>2. Start the server</h2>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`bunx rob-mcp\n# Plain Node is supported too:\nnpx -y rob-mcp`}
    label="Run stdio MCP"
  />
  <h2>3. Add it to your MCP client</h2>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`{
  "mcpServers": {
    "rob-mcp": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "rob-mcp"],
      "env": {
        "RPC_URL_4663": "\${RPC_URL_4663}"
      }
    }
  }
}`}
    label="Client configuration"
  />
  <h2>4. Make the first call</h2>
  <p>
    Ask your client to call <code>list_stock_tokens</code> with <code
      >{"{"}"search":"AAPL"{"}"}</code
    >. It is implemented, free, and does not require a price-liveness source.
  </p>
  <div class="callout">
    The server verifies the RPC’s live chain ID at boot. A URL for the wrong chain fails closed.
  </div>
</DocLayout>
